  "releaseNotes": "Touch feedback: a visual indicator per active contact (appears on\n\t\t\tTouchBegin, follows moves, fades out on TouchEnd), enabled by default\n\t\t\t(DrmTouchOptions.ShowTouchFeedback / DRMKIT_TOUCH_FEEDBACK), plus soft\n\t\t\tcursor hiding while any contact is active (HideCursorWhileTouching /\n\t\t\tDRMKIT_TOUCH_HIDE_CURSOR). SYN_DROPPED recovery now re-announces\n\t\t\tphysically held contacts via EVIOCGMTSLOTS instead of leaving them\n\t\t\tdead until re-touch. /dev/input hotplug via inotify: new event*\n\t\t\tdevices start readers at runtime, removed devices are cleaned up and\n\t\t\ttheir contacts cancelled (vanished-device readers exit cleanly).\n\t\t\tPerf: all events of one evdev SYN_REPORT frame are dispatched as a\n\t\t\tsingle UI post, in order.",
